WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:49.900
"The Forbidden Sacred Ground!

3
00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:54.090
<b>Divine Reckoning</b>

4
00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:54.150
The Island Where God Lives
and Heaven's Judgement!"

5
00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:56.660
There's actually a God?!

6
00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:58.280
And he lives on an
island up here

7
00:01:58.370 --> 00:02:00.620
that no one's
allowed to walk on?

8
00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:04.090
He does.

9
00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:05.470
I'm sure that everyone
noticed the big sign

10
00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:07.260
that said "Godland Skypiea."

11
00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:11.310
That means this land is ruled
by the almighty God Eneru.

12
00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:13.520
God's name is Eneru?

13
00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:18.520
He knows and sees everything.
He's truly omniscient.

14
00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:20.020
Everything?

15
00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:24.130
He keeps his all-seeing eyes
focused on everyone. Always.

16
00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.010
For real?

17
00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:26.010
Like right now?

18
00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:27.550
Oh, yes.

19
00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:30.730
I hate it when people stare
at me and I can't see them!

20
00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:34.110
I can't get over
the size of those trees.

21
00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:35.570
Wait a minute.

22
00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:39.370
So they do have earthen
ground up here.

23
00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:45.790
I see.

24
00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:48.620
A place we're not allowed to
go to no matter what, huh?

25
00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:49.880
Ah!

26
00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:50.980
I've seen that look in
your eyes before, Luffy,

27
00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:52.250
and it always gets
us into trouble!

28
00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:53.750
When the lady says
we can't go there

29
00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:56.260
because it's sacred or whatever,
that's exactly what she means!

30
00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:57.630
We cannot go there!

31
00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:59.760
I am not letting you drag me
down with you this time!

32
00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:02.640
No. Hey. Heh.

33
00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:05.070
I understand we're not
supposed to go there.

34
00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:09.320
Come on!

35
00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:13.120
You really think I'm the kinda
guy who would do that? Heh.

36
00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:15.790
– Yes. Absolutely.
– Yes. Absolutely.

37
00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.300
Hey, wait.

38
00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:19.760
If this guy is God, then
shouldn't he forgive you

39
00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:21.090
no matter what you do?

40
00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:22.720
Walking around on some
forbidden island

41
00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.300
doesn't seem like
a big deal to me.

42
00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:25.470
No.

43
00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:27.220
Breaking any law set
forth by our almighty

44
00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:29.770
is nothing less than sacrilege.

45
00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:32.330
So I guess it
doesn't matter either way.

46
00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:35.920
He'd go even if it
meant he'd die in the process.

47
00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:38.470
Nami! Nami...

48
00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:40.350
All right. Let's go
and find her!

49
00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:41.520
We're wasting time!

50
00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:42.810
You don't care
about saving Nami!

51
00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:44.600
You just wanna satisfy
your twisted urge

52
00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:47.600
to do the exact opposite
of what you've been told!

53
00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:54.460
Those are the biggest
trees I've ever seen in my life.

54
00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:56.420
They've gotta be
hundreds of years old.

55
00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:00.250
That, or things grow bigger
a few miles up in the sky.

56
00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.710
And they're so tall.

57
00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:06.560
I can't even see
where they top out.

58
00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.130
Luffy, we gotta get going.

59
00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:13.590
Yeah, I know.
Just gimme a second.

60
00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:15.140
Fine. Don't listen to me.

61
00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:17.260
But you're gonna feel awful
if something bad happens to Nami

62
00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:19.350
while you're busy
stuffing your face.

63
00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:21.430
The food'll be here
when we get back!

64
00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:23.640
Mh-hm. I'm right behind you.

65
00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:25.980
Conis, I know this guy,

66
00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:27.450
and I could be here
all day waiting on him.

67
00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:29.120
Could you tell me how to
get to the Upper Yard?

68
00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:30.750
I gotta go help Nami.

69
00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:32.830
But you don't know for sure.

70
00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:33.750
Hm?

71
00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:34.840
About Nami.

72
00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:36.050
She might just be
out on the clouds

73
00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:37.970
and nowhere near the Upper Yard.

74
00:04:38.050 --> 00:04:39.380
I mean...

75
00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:43.390
I can't explain how
devastating it could be to us

76
00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:45.930
to incur the wrath
of our God Eneru.

77
00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:49.190
Help!

78
00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:55.110
Somebody help me!

79
00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:00.350
I can't live like this!

80
00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:01.430
What's your problem?

81
00:05:01.510 --> 00:05:02.890
I'm nervous.

82
00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:28.420
Oh, no!

83
00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:40.280
Bastard. He took my prey.

84
00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:44.700
Those voices. Those sounds.

85
00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:47.000
What were they?

86
00:05:49.670 --> 00:05:51.590
Just give up!

87
00:05:51.670 --> 00:05:53.170
You should do the same.

88
00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:55.300
This boy is mine! Ha-ha!

89
00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:56.590
Not if I can help it!

90
00:05:56.670 --> 00:05:59.680
Oh, but it doesn't
look like you can!

91
00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:11.310
Wait. What the...?

92
00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:13.060
Who are they?

93
00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:15.280
Something tells me
I don't wanna find out.

94
00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:16.990
What's going on?

95
00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:20.780
Hmm. So this is
your old waver, huh?

96
00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:23.420
You should take
better care of it.

97
00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:25.630
It's not ours. We found
it like that that.

98
00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:27.630
Would you like me
to take a look at it?

99
00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:30.680
Assuming it's fixable, I should
be able to do that for you.

100
00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:33.410
I'm an engineer that
specializes in dial ships,

101
00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:34.690
so I should know.

102
00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:20.130
What the...?

103
00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:25.800
You, down there, help!

104
00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:28.180
Please, give me a ride! Please!

105
00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:31.930
You want a ride? But this
is a one person boat.

106
00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:33.140
Please help me!

107
00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:36.350
Oh, I can't. There's no room.

108
00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:39.100
Either give me the boat
or I'll slice you up!

109
00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:42.480
Guerilla!

110
00:07:45.670 --> 00:07:47.010
No.

111
00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:09.680
Is this Eneru's doing?

112
00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:21.350
How dare you harm Vearth!

113
00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:05.440
Get some water
dials down here now!

114
00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:08.050
The fire's spreading!

115
00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:13.280
<b>Lovely Street
Angel Island</b>

116
00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:14.980
Form up. Salute!

117
00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:17.230
– Heso!
– Heso!

118
00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:21.670
<b>Captain McKinley
White Berets, Skypiea Police</b>

119
00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:21.660
Good day. Heso!

120
00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:23.670
What are the White
Berets doing here?

121
00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:26.000
Oh, no, something
must've happened.

122
00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:28.880
You are all warned to
use extreme caution!

123
00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:30.800
I've received word
that illegal entrants

124
00:09:30.860 --> 00:09:35.410
have infiltrated Skypiea
through Angel Beach today.

125
00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:38.080
There are reportedly
seven suspects!

126
00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:39.330
But do not worry!

127
00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:41.050
You can help with our
search and investigation

128
00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:43.070
by reporting all
suspicious activity!

129
00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:45.370
Leave it to the White Berets!

130
00:09:47.240 --> 00:09:49.450
– White Berets!
– White Berets!

131
00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:50.830
Did you see that?

132
00:09:50.910 --> 00:09:53.580
It appeared as if he was talking
to someone in the water.

133
00:09:53.670 --> 00:09:55.660
He was probably delusional.

134
00:09:55.660 --> 00:09:58.670
Would someone
please shut that dog up?

135
00:09:58.920 --> 00:10:01.170
He was most likely
begging for his life.

136
00:10:02.630 --> 00:10:05.090
Why did Eneru take
care of that guy himself?

137
00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:08.300
Isn't that why he sent us
here in the first place?

138
00:10:08.430 --> 00:10:10.570
We probably ran out of time.

139
00:10:10.570 --> 00:10:11.630
Ran out of time?

140
00:10:12.510 --> 00:10:14.020
Yet another
group of illegal entrants

141
00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:16.890
have already
infiltrated Skypiea.

142
00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:18.270
Again?

143
00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:20.360
Old lady Amazon
informed us that it's a ship

144
00:10:20.440 --> 00:10:23.110
with seven Blue Sea
dwellers on board.

145
00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:25.450
Seven Blue Sea dwellers?

146
00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:27.420
That's probably us!

147
00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:29.210
We're here illeagally?

148
00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:31.160
But if you wish to proceed,

149
00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:32.910
you must first pay
the entrance fee

150
00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:35.210
of one billion
extols per person.

151
00:10:35.290 --> 00:10:37.210
That is the law.

152
00:10:38.800 --> 00:10:43.870
Because we didn't pay
the entrance fee? No way!

153
00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:45.290
Seven heads.

154
00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:48.410
Looks like one of us is
gonna have to share.

155
00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:51.210
What the heck is
happening on this island?

156
00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:53.300
And who are those people?

157
00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:56.130
This is crazy!

158
00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:07.060
I need to get back to
the others to warn them.

159
00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:09.930
I just hope I get to them
before it's too late.

160
00:11:16.290 --> 00:11:17.610
Beat this one, Usopp! Look!

161
00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:20.110
I don't think that'll
be a problem!

162
00:11:24.010 --> 00:11:27.220
See? My cloud sculpture's so
good it should be in a museum!

163
00:11:28.430 --> 00:11:29.670
That's amazing!

164
00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:32.040
That's the worst looking
art I've ever seen!

165
00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:33.840
So can you fix it?

166
00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:36.420
I've never seen
parts like these before.

167
00:11:36.510 --> 00:11:38.220
Come on, just fix it already!

168
00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:39.880
I'm sorry,
but until I have a chance

169
00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:42.550
to look at this closer,
I don't know if I can fix it.

170
00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:43.850
Will you at least try?

171
00:11:43.890 --> 00:11:45.440
Yes, of course.

172
00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:51.240
Huh?

173
00:11:51.330 --> 00:11:53.080
Looks like we have company.

174
00:12:00.670 --> 00:12:02.500
You there! On the beach!

175
00:12:02.590 --> 00:12:03.800
Don't move!

176
00:12:03.850 --> 00:12:06.390
Does he mean us?

177
00:12:18.250 --> 00:12:20.960
Hey, uh...
why are they crawling?

178
00:12:21.150 --> 00:12:22.150
Who knows?

179
00:12:22.230 --> 00:12:25.150
I mean, they've
obviously got issues.

180
00:12:25.240 --> 00:12:28.820
Because they're
crawling around like crabs?

181
00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:32.170
White berets, halt!

182
00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:35.630
– Heso!
– Heso!

183
00:12:35.720 --> 00:12:36.550
Heso.

184
00:12:36.620 --> 00:12:37.540
Heso, gentlemen.

185
00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:39.170
Suu-suu.

186
00:12:39.260 --> 00:12:41.970
Speak our language!
We can't understand you.

187
00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:43.670
What are they? Soldiers?

188
00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:45.720
Usopp said they have issues.

189
00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:47.680
Well, look what we have here.

190
00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:49.390
You must be the
Blue Sea dwellers

191
00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:52.270
who have illegally entered the
sovereign land of Skypiea!

192
00:12:52.350 --> 00:12:53.560
– Huh?
– Huh?

193
00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:55.480
Prepare to have the weight
of Heaven's Judgment

194
00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:57.400
brought down upon you!

195
00:12:57.750 --> 00:12:59.290
You're calling them criminals?

196
00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:01.210
Illegal entry? What's that?

197
00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:03.340
Don't waste your
breath making excuses.

198
00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:05.840
Amazon, the woman who
stands at Heaven's Gate,

199
00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:08.880
captured these very images
using her vision dial.

200
00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:11.180
No, wait. That can't be!

201
00:13:11.260 --> 00:13:13.220
I think this is all
a big misunderstanding,

202
00:13:13.280 --> 00:13:14.700
Captain McKinley.

203
00:13:14.740 --> 00:13:17.490
They're not the criminals
you're making them out to be.

204
00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:19.710
What do you mean
by illegal entry?

205
00:13:19.790 --> 00:13:21.790
Does this have to do
with that ridiculous

206
00:13:21.830 --> 00:13:23.580
one billion extol entrance fee?

207
00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:25.120
Because we didn't
pay her a thing.

208
00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:27.470
But didn't that old lady say
we didn't have to pay it?

209
00:13:27.550 --> 00:13:29.300
It's not like she
tried to stop us.

210
00:13:29.380 --> 00:13:30.470
Yeah, that's true!

211
00:13:30.550 --> 00:13:33.260
Enough! There's no sense
trying to deny it.

212
00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:34.420
Now, fess up!

213
00:13:34.420 --> 00:13:37.170
Don't worry, you need not
become panicked just yet.

214
00:13:37.260 --> 00:13:38.550
According to Heaven's Judgment,

215
00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:41.430
Illegal Entry is only
an 11th degree crime!

216
00:13:41.510 --> 00:13:43.100
Once you accept
your punishment...

217
00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:44.180
which will be minimal...

218
00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:46.220
you become legal
tourists on the spot

219
00:13:46.310 --> 00:13:47.850
and may go about your business.

220
00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:49.850
Well, you shoulda
told us that sooner,

221
00:13:49.950 --> 00:13:51.320
but before we accept,

222
00:13:51.410 --> 00:13:53.530
what exactly do you have
planned as far as punishment?

223
00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:54.990
A mere slap on the wrist.

224
00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:58.040
All you need to do is pay
ten times the entrance fee.

225
00:13:58.130 --> 00:13:59.840
Of course, if you
pay immediately,

226
00:13:59.920 --> 00:14:02.250
we'll pretend this little
episode never happened.

227
00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:05.590
So, ten billion per person,
times seven people

228
00:14:05.670 --> 00:14:08.340
makes your total
70 billion extols.

229
00:14:08.420 --> 00:14:09.250
Cash only.

230
00:14:09.330 --> 00:14:11.710
Wait, 70 billion extols?

231
00:14:12.060 --> 00:14:13.980
That sounds like an
awful lotta money!

232
00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:15.460
How much is that in berries?

233
00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:18.050
That's the currency used
in the Blue Sea World, right?

234
00:14:18.130 --> 00:14:21.550
Today's exchange rates are
10,000 extols per berry.

235
00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:23.590
Let's see now,
there's, uh, 10,000,

236
00:14:23.680 --> 00:14:25.180
and you gotta carry
the one, and, uh,

237
00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:26.750
is there a decimal in there?

238
00:14:26.830 --> 00:14:28.210
Five?

239
00:14:28.270 --> 00:14:31.230
Seventy billion extols is seven
million berries, genius.

240
00:14:31.310 --> 00:14:34.400
Get real! Do you realize
how expensive that is?!

241
00:14:34.480 --> 00:14:36.480
After risking our lives
coming to this place,

242
00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:38.140
why should we have
to pay a stupid fee

243
00:14:38.230 --> 00:14:40.100
just to enter your
precious city?

244
00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:41.440
We can't agree to that!

245
00:14:41.570 --> 00:14:43.240
You brought this on yourselves.

246
00:14:43.340 --> 00:14:46.720
If you had just paid the 700,000
Berries in the first place,

247
00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:48.410
we wouldn't be having this talk.

248
00:14:48.490 --> 00:14:51.660
That's still way too expensive!

249
00:14:51.770 --> 00:14:53.310
This is your first warning.

250
00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:57.210
The White Berets serve under
the vassals of almighty Eneru.

251
00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:59.880
Arguing with us will only raise
the level of your crime.

252
00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:02.300
Oh, whatever, man.

253
00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:03.760
Let's forget these idiots.

254
00:15:03.810 --> 00:15:05.850
We need to start looking for
Nami. I'm getting worried.

255
00:15:05.930 --> 00:15:08.480
She may need my tender
affections right about now.

256
00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:09.420
Is she in trouble?

257
00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:10.800
I doubt it.

258
00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:18.850
Those weird guys
from earlier somehow knew

259
00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:20.890
about us coming to Skypiea.

260
00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:23.560
That means Luffy and the
others may be in trouble.

261
00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:25.270
Better hurry back!

262
00:15:29.020 --> 00:15:31.050
I can't wait to ride this thing!

263
00:15:31.050 --> 00:15:32.910
I hope you can fix it.

264
00:15:34.380 --> 00:15:36.340
This waver
looks downright abused!

265
00:15:36.420 --> 00:15:39.010
If I find out you're responsible
for this damage,

266
00:15:39.090 --> 00:15:41.470
you're looking at a
tenth degree crime:

267
00:15:41.590 --> 00:15:43.510
"Destruction of Sky
Island Property

268
00:15:43.600 --> 00:15:44.850
by a Blue Sea Dweller."

269
00:15:44.930 --> 00:15:47.100
I'm sorry, Captain McKinley,
this is my fault.

270
00:15:47.180 --> 00:15:49.140
I crashed the waver, not him.

271
00:15:49.230 --> 00:15:50.980
Yeah, besides,
this thing's mine.

272
00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:53.840
Is that right?
Sounds suspicious to me.

273
00:15:53.920 --> 00:15:56.220
I was under the impression
wavers didn't exist

274
00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:57.300
in the Blue Sea World.

275
00:15:57.390 --> 00:15:59.430
If this one was stolen
from Skypiea,

276
00:15:59.510 --> 00:16:01.220
the degree of your
crime will increase!

277
00:16:01.310 --> 00:16:04.270
It's not stolen!
Wanna fight about it?

278
00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:06.190
Excuse me?

279
00:16:06.930 --> 00:16:09.520
Oh, no, there's
a whole group of people!

280
00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:12.270
I hope they're not
those guys from before.

281
00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:13.610
Whoever they are,

282
00:16:13.690 --> 00:16:16.280
I hope Luffy's not pulling
any of his usual stunts.

283
00:16:16.360 --> 00:16:18.240
Let's sit down and take
a breather, okay?

284
00:16:18.300 --> 00:16:20.220
Zoro, Luffy, Chopper,
there's no reason for us...

285
00:16:20.300 --> 00:16:22.210
I'm back!

286
00:16:22.300 --> 00:16:25.510
Nami, baby! I missed you!

287
00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:29.430
Luffy! Promise you won't
start any trouble, okay?!

288
00:16:29.510 --> 00:16:31.180
Don't know if I
can keep that promise!

289
00:16:31.180 --> 00:16:32.640
Hey! Nami!

290
00:16:32.730 --> 00:16:35.020
We need you to fork up seven
million berries from your stash

291
00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:36.780
to pay for all the fines we got!

292
00:16:36.860 --> 00:16:39.730
Oh, good! So we pay the
fine and we're clear?

293
00:16:39.730 --> 00:16:42.820
Did he say seven million?

294
00:16:46.370 --> 00:16:47.480
Hm? What?!

295
00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:50.070
You're ripping us off!

296
00:16:57.780 --> 00:16:59.150
Oh, crap!

297
00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:01.870
I was so worked up I forgot
to hit the brakes!

298
00:17:01.980 --> 00:17:02.810
– Ouch.
– Ouch.

299
00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:04.700
– Captain!
– Captain!

300
00:17:04.780 --> 00:17:06.280
Hey, thanks for letting
me use your waver.

301
00:17:06.340 --> 00:17:07.920
I love the way it handles.

302
00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:09.460
I'm glad you enjoyed it.

303
00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:10.670
But more importantly,

304
00:17:10.760 --> 00:17:12.720
do you realize how much
trouble you're in now?

305
00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:13.890
Captain...

306
00:17:13.970 --> 00:17:15.390
Guys, let's make
ourselves scarce.

307
00:17:15.470 --> 00:17:16.560
Aww. Aren't you gonna finish

308
00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:17.810
the fight you just started?

309
00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:19.730
Trust me, this
Eneru is not someone

310
00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:20.660
we wanna mess with.

311
00:17:20.660 --> 00:17:22.120
Oh, yes, quite.

312
00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:24.750
And knocking out an official
is a crime of the fifth degree.

313
00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:28.190
Once you're found guilty of
committing a fifth degree crime,

314
00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:29.820
almighty Eneru will banish you

315
00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:31.780
to the land of the
drifting clouds.

316
00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:33.200
How's that bad?

317
00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:35.160
Land of the drifting clouds?

318
00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:36.870
That sounds like fun!

319
00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:39.500
It's a death sentence. You die!

320
00:17:39.630 --> 00:17:41.760
They'll put you and your
ship on a small cloud

321
00:17:41.840 --> 00:17:43.340
and set you adrift in the sea

322
00:17:43.430 --> 00:17:45.970
with no chance of
rescue or escape.

323
00:17:46.050 --> 00:17:49.640
You'll eventually die a very
slow and painful death.

324
00:17:49.720 --> 00:17:51.520
It's terrible!

325
00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:52.910
Interesting.

326
00:17:52.990 --> 00:17:55.620
That must be why we saw
that ship fall from the sky.

327
00:17:55.690 --> 00:17:57.440
Wait, what are you
talking about?

328
00:17:57.520 --> 00:17:59.860
Don't you remember that
galleon we saw falling?

329
00:17:59.940 --> 00:18:02.320
The St. Briss,
I think it was called.

330
00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:03.690
For all we know,

331
00:18:03.780 --> 00:18:06.320
that crew could've been
punished over 200 years ago.

332
00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:13.280
– You! Criminals!
– You! Criminals!

333
00:18:13.360 --> 00:18:15.660
Do you scum know
what you've done to our Captain?

334
00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:16.530
Who cares?

335
00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:18.200
Sanji, let me handle this.

336
00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:19.580
Anything for you!

337
00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:22.420
Don't take it so personally.
It was a lucky shot!

338
00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:23.780
A lucky shot?

339
00:18:23.860 --> 00:18:25.700
Completely unintentional!

340
00:18:25.780 --> 00:18:26.870
You're lying!

341
00:18:26.950 --> 00:18:28.440
No, I'm telling you the truth.

342
00:18:28.440 --> 00:18:30.230
but can you blame a
beginner for messing up

343
00:18:30.320 --> 00:18:32.070
and nearly killing your boss?

344
00:18:32.150 --> 00:18:33.400
That's weird,
seemed like you had

345
00:18:33.490 --> 00:18:35.030
a pretty good handle
on it to me.

346
00:18:35.110 --> 00:18:36.450
Shuddup!

347
00:18:36.530 --> 00:18:37.990
Quiet, Luffy!

348
00:18:38.070 --> 00:18:40.490
Nami's trying to trick them into
thinking it was an accident.

349
00:18:40.580 --> 00:18:41.950
Don't blow it, okay?

350
00:18:42.040 --> 00:18:43.160
All right!

351
00:18:43.210 --> 00:18:44.250
Gentlemen.

352
00:18:44.330 --> 00:18:46.000
As important as your
investigation is,

353
00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:49.090
perhaps it would be best to get
the captain to a doctor first.

354
00:18:49.210 --> 00:18:50.250
Just a thought.

355
00:18:50.300 --> 00:18:52.760
Oh. Right! The captain!

356
00:18:52.820 --> 00:18:54.240
Now, there's no reason to panic.

357
00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:55.950
Let's take him to my house.

358
00:18:55.960 --> 00:18:57.290
We'll get right on that.

359
00:18:57.350 --> 00:18:58.640
– Heso!
– Heso!

360
00:19:01.020 --> 00:19:01.980
Consider yourselves under

361
00:19:02.060 --> 00:19:03.230
preliminary arrest.

362
00:19:03.270 --> 00:19:05.270
Don't go anywhere! Got it?

363
00:19:05.400 --> 00:19:08.400
The poor captain's bleeding!

364
00:19:08.490 --> 00:19:09.740
Why are they crawling again?

365
00:19:10.680 --> 00:19:12.300
Can't they just carry him
like normal people?

366
00:19:12.510 --> 00:19:13.760
You guys saved my life,

367
00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:16.600
so I know you're not as bad
as they claim you are.

368
00:19:16.710 --> 00:19:19.170
So take this chance
and get out of here!

369
00:19:19.250 --> 00:19:20.590
Wait!

370
00:19:21.980 --> 00:19:24.850
I think we'd
better take her advice.

371
00:19:24.940 --> 00:19:27.190
When I was on the waver,
I saw it for myself.

372
00:19:27.270 --> 00:19:29.610
An island filled with monsters!

373
00:19:29.700 --> 00:19:31.660
Great, so you did
exactly what everyone

374
00:19:31.740 --> 00:19:33.160
was hoping you wouldn't do.

375
00:19:33.250 --> 00:19:36.010
You mean the place we were
told to never ever set foot on?

376
00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:36.900
And there's monsters?

377
00:19:36.980 --> 00:19:39.900
Whoa! Don't give 'im any ideas!

378
00:19:40.010 --> 00:19:41.760
It's nothing to get
excited about, Luffy.

379
00:19:41.840 --> 00:19:44.300
The last thing we need is
to get involved with this.

380
00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:47.080
Regardless, we're
leaving, now let's go!

381
00:19:47.170 --> 00:19:49.630
Ah, it'll break my
heart to be away from Conis,

382
00:19:49.800 --> 00:19:51.410
but if that's what
Nami wants, so be it.

383
00:19:51.840 --> 00:19:53.200
If we stick around any longer,

384
00:19:53.200 --> 00:19:55.950
Conis and Pagaya may get
in trouble because of us.

385
00:19:56.220 --> 00:19:57.300
That's true.

386
00:19:57.450 --> 00:19:59.790
Those White Berets will charge
them as our accomplices!

387
00:19:59.870 --> 00:20:01.500
If we can escape now on our own,

388
00:20:01.580 --> 00:20:03.540
then it shouldn't cause
them any trouble, right?

389
00:20:03.630 --> 00:20:05.090
After all, how can
they be helping us

390
00:20:05.150 --> 00:20:06.530
when they're with that captain?

391
00:20:06.610 --> 00:20:09.570
Okay, that's the plan. Let's go!

392
00:20:14.250 --> 00:20:16.490
Luffy, what are you doing?

393
00:20:16.490 --> 00:20:17.780
Why are we running away?

394
00:20:18.160 --> 00:20:20.070
They haven't done anything.

395
00:20:20.210 --> 00:20:21.220
Whoever arrests
them is an idiot.

396
00:20:21.220 --> 00:20:23.340
I know that, but...

397
00:20:25.900 --> 00:20:28.420
Please. Please hurry.

398
00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:31.630
The Blue Sea dwellers
will never escape!

399
00:20:36.030 --> 00:20:38.530
Can't you two argue on
the boat? Come on!

400
00:20:38.620 --> 00:20:40.450
How many times do
I have to tell you?!

401
00:20:40.570 --> 00:20:44.490
Staying here equals more
trouble for everybody!

402
00:20:44.600 --> 00:20:46.270
We're in trouble no matter what.

403
00:20:47.450 --> 00:20:49.290
Save yourselves!

404
00:20:49.340 --> 00:20:50.340
Please, go!

405
00:20:50.420 --> 00:20:51.960
Ugh. Just great.

406
00:20:52.040 --> 00:20:53.160
Be careful, miss.

407
00:20:53.250 --> 00:20:55.040
If you say anything to
defend these criminals,

408
00:20:55.120 --> 00:20:58.250
I will consider you and
your father accomplices.

409
00:20:58.330 --> 00:21:01.590
These people must be punished
to the full extent of the law

410
00:21:01.690 --> 00:21:05.070
for all the abusive language
and deplorable violence.

411
00:21:05.150 --> 00:21:08.910
I find them guilty of
fifth degree crimes.

412
00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:10.740
In the name of almighty Eneru,

413
00:21:10.800 --> 00:21:14.850
you are banished to drift
in the clouds for eternity.

414
00:21:14.950 --> 00:21:16.790
I told you, it was an accident!

415
00:21:16.870 --> 00:21:18.370
Oh. Forget it.

416
00:21:18.450 --> 00:21:20.210
Arrest them!

417
00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:23.920
Just run! You can't win!

418
00:21:26.170 --> 00:21:28.840
Fire the milky arrows!

419
00:21:30.070 --> 00:21:31.240
Go, Nami! Run!

420
00:21:31.320 --> 00:21:32.660
Ya think?

421
00:21:36.080 --> 00:21:37.330
What the heck?

422
00:21:37.410 --> 00:21:39.870
Clouds?

423
00:21:41.920 --> 00:21:44.730
White Berets! Attack!

424
00:21:55.830 --> 00:21:57.460
Cool trick! Mind if I try?

425
00:22:03.190 --> 00:22:04.110
Whoa!

426
00:22:09.600 --> 00:22:11.270
You see his arm?

427
00:22:11.360 --> 00:22:13.320
Look! He's all stretchy!

428
00:22:13.400 --> 00:22:14.480
I hope he's okay!

429
00:22:16.740 --> 00:22:20.030
Gum-Gum...

430
00:22:20.030 --> 00:22:22.400
No way! devil fruit!

431
00:22:22.620 --> 00:22:25.950
...Fireworks!

432
00:23:01.320 --> 00:23:03.410
Piece of cake.

433
00:23:03.500 --> 00:23:06.580
Nami! How's the money
situation looking?

434
00:23:06.670 --> 00:23:08.380
Fifty thousand berries left!

435
00:23:08.460 --> 00:23:11.050
Fifty thousand?
We're that broke?

436
00:23:11.130 --> 00:23:14.010
Normally that'd last
us a day or two at most.

437
00:23:14.090 --> 00:23:16.260
What's the deal?
Why are we so poor?

438
00:23:16.340 --> 00:23:19.010
Listen up, everybody! Your
captain has something to say!

439
00:23:19.100 --> 00:23:21.060
Everyone on my ship
needs to be more good

440
00:23:21.140 --> 00:23:22.100
with money from now on!

441
00:23:22.190 --> 00:23:23.730
So lead by example!

442
00:23:23.880 --> 00:23:24.680
Huh?!

443
00:23:25.810 --> 00:23:27.730
In any case,
the Fighting Formation B

444
00:23:27.810 --> 00:23:29.560
I taught them to use
was successful.

445
00:23:29.640 --> 00:23:30.400
There's that.

446
00:23:30.400 --> 00:23:31.570
Really?

447
00:23:31.770 --> 00:23:33.400
They defeated the White Berets.

448
00:23:33.480 --> 00:23:35.020
Unbelievable!

449
00:23:35.020 --> 00:23:36.890
At this altitude,
the athletic ability

450
00:23:36.980 --> 00:23:40.230
of Blue Sea dwellers
usually decreases.

451
00:23:45.560 --> 00:23:47.940
Those poor deluded fools.

452
00:23:48.070 --> 00:23:51.200
Sorry, criminals!
You have no chance of escape!

453
00:23:51.280 --> 00:23:52.280
Hm?

454
00:23:52.380 --> 00:23:53.540
You should have behaved

455
00:23:53.620 --> 00:23:56.250
and done what I told you to do.

456
00:23:56.330 --> 00:23:59.620
Of all the upholders
of Law here in Skypiea,

457
00:23:59.680 --> 00:24:02.140
we White Berets are
the most lenient.

458
00:24:02.220 --> 00:24:06.650
However, they are not
nearly as forgiving!

459
00:24:08.610 --> 00:24:10.110
Congratulations!

460
00:24:10.190 --> 00:24:13.610
You are now considered
second degree criminals.

461
00:24:13.690 --> 00:24:16.150
You can try to cry for mercy...

462
00:24:18.150 --> 00:24:20.700
...but you will all be judged...

463
00:24:21.500 --> 00:24:23.810
...by the Priests of Upper Yard!

464
00:24:23.810 --> 00:24:25.490
Heso!
